  "text": "Prophylactic cranial irradiation (PCI) (25Gy in 10 fractions over 2 weeks, on 5 consecutive days a week) was administered to responding patients who had a negative MR brain scan after completion of TRT and all chemotherapy. Parallel opposing fields were used, with 6 MV X-ray a linear accelerator. The whole brain was irradiated (with the inferior border following a line drawn to avoid the eyes), including the temporal fossae and the intracranial portion of the cranial nerves."
