  "style": "",
  "text": "As regard to optimal timing of TRT related to induction chemotherapy, a Korean randomized trial compared TRT in the first versus third cycle of chemotherapy for LS-SCLS and found the third-cycle approach was noninferior in treatment compliance and clinical outcomes, with lower toxic effects [17]. Multi-cycles of chemotherapy might also allow time to prepare TRT. Given the large tumor burden, all patients had to complete 3-4 cycles of induction chemotherapy before TRT; although excessive chemotherapy might prolong treatment and affect efficacy, a few ultimately received 4 cycles because of bulky tumors and low response to chemotherapy. Multivariate Cox regression analysis revealed no significant difference in PFS and OS between induction chemotherapy cycles (Supplementary materials). Compared with the Korean study's late TRT arm, concurrent TRT after induction chemotherapy here yielded better PFS (median, 26.0 versus 11.2 months) and OS (median, 35.0 versus 26.8 months). All patients achieved cCR or cPR after induction chemotherapy and then received IMRT-based TRT, possibly contributing to these favorable outcomes."
